WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.250
What was that?

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:08.000
Wouldn't it be in the Alliance's best interests
to ally ourselves with that mage Siluca?

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.260
If we recognized a Lord who expanded
his territories after claiming to be with the Union,

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.510
we'd have little hope of suppressing
a surge of like-minded Lords

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.520
If I act on your advice, I will have
no choice but to attack Theo Cornaro.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.860
Your adopted daughter will surely
share a fate with her Lord.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.400
You're sure of this?

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.570
I am prepared for that.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.040
Our decision is as follows.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.540
Theo Cornaro's request to pledge allegiance,
as well as to join the Alliance...

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:48.920
...is denied.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.890
I advise that he forfeit his territories and
court rank, and quickly depart from Savis.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:57.640
Otherwise...

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:03.230
The Valdrind Order of Knights will arrive
in full force to regain the King of Savis's lands,

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.480
and subjugate Viscount Theo Cornaro.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.480
You overplayed your hand, you see.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.740
Unfortunately, I cannot follow your advice.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.830
The next time we meet
will be on the battlefield.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:56.300
Unbelievable!

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:01.760
Sure, I get that a contracted mage
must set aside his personal feelings.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.430
But he takes it way too far!

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.100
Don't be so harsh on Father.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.060
If the Alliance won't have us,
then we'll just lean on the Union.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.020
Villar Constance...

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.520
You really think the Lustful Earl
will take our side?

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:23.830
Margaret?

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.660
The earl says he has no intention
of meeting with you now.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.540
I know that your bid
to join the Alliance fell through,

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.840
but you have some nerve to show up here!

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:40.510
When Plan A doesn't work out,
the only option is to go with Plan B.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.970
If Lord Theo manages to survive,
the Kreische family's prestige will be sullied,

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:49.480
and that will allow us to hold back
the Alliance's resolve.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.730
Do you really think
saving your Lord will help the earl?

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.320
No.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.570
If he does not, then it won't be long
before the earl is destroyed.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:01.820
You little brat!

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:08.950
Lord Villar is a capable warrior, and won't
lose easily to the Lords of the Alliance.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.960
You mean that Lustful Earl–

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:17.090
Lord Villar is well aware of what
those at the Magic Academy call him.

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:21.380
However, there are many in Artuk
who believe in witchcraft.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.470
And it's out of consideration for his people
that the earl contracts with female mages.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:31.140
But I hear he dissolves those contracts
once they're past 25.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.360
If they were bound for their entire lives,
they could never marry nor bear children.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.020
The earl would pity anyone
who ended up that way.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.910
The Margrave of Valdrind will be launching
an attack on us with the King of Savis.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:55.170
And we will counterattack from this castle.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.920
They have at least 20,000 troops on their side.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.550
And we've got maybe 3,000?

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.930
Not only that, but we're up against
Valdrind's knights-at-arms, eh?

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.180
Confronting them head-on
won't get us anywhere!

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:12.810
Right, so that's why we're going for a siege.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.480
Sir Lassic will take the West Gate.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.980
Sir Neyman, the East Gate.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.940
And Aishela and the mercenaries,
please defend the south front gate.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.870
If they see we're a force to be reckoned with,
even if we end up surrendering,

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.950
we can get them to meet
some of our conditions!

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:38.000
Let's all work a miracle!

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:39.540
Yeah!

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.060
They're not at full strength?

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.190
Are they wary of reinforcements
sent by the Earl of Artuk?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.400
But they have no way of knowing
that our talks broke down.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.820
I'm counting on you, everyone...

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.460
Commence attack!

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.060
We won't hold out for too long, eh?

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:39.310
Everyone, withdraw!
Wait for Siluca's orders!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.110
Allow me to guide you...

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.320
...to the afterlife!

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:32.620
Aishela!

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:36.830
Are you all right?

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:39.370
I think my number's up.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:42.040
I'm going ahead of you,

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:45.670
but you don't have to come, okay?

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.800
Aishela!

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:51.840
Don't die on me! Open your eyes!

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.600
I will heal that person.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:05.900
You still have a mission to fulfill.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.240
You must remain on this land.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.580
Take care of Aishela.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.590
Now!

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:37.310
Let's go!

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:51.650
Fall back! Fall back!

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:56.990
Lord Theo!

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.080
We held them off somehow, huh?

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:02.370
Yeah.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:03.210
Lord Theo!

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:06.330
Here is the latest.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.710
Sir Neyman was killed in action
at the East Gate.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:10.380
Sir Neyman?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.210
No way...

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.340
They're struggling at the West Gate.
It's been breached, and Sir Lassic is retreating.

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:17.850
Even Lassic?

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:21.770
Irvin! Captain Gluck!

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.320
Fall back! Retreat to the castle!

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:34.070
Everyone attack!

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.330
Sir Lassic, I think it's time.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.960
Change of plans! We counterattack here!

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.680
If it's one-on-one, Lassic can't be beaten.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:58.850
Fall back!

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:01.470
We'll overwhelm them with numbers
where there's more room!

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:07.480
Wha...

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.710
They're cutting off our retreat?

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:39.260
Give me that!

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:43.310
King of Savis! Prepare to die!

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:45.730
Don't give me that, punk!

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.950
To think you'd slay the King of Savis!

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:50.670
I'd like to offer the troops I seized
to you, Lord Theo.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.630
No. I want you to hold onto them.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.460
Why?

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:59.920
In a sense, your defeat of the King of Savis
made this a victory for us.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:05.930
And so the next step of our strategy
will be to broker a ceasefire.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:10.690
Now, under what kind of conditions
would Valdrind agree to withdraw?

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:15.860
That would be for Lord Theo to retain the
minimum court rank, and to leave this region.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:21.200
And for all of the Savis Lords
to be directly subjugated by Valdrind.

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:26.950
Sir Lassic, we'd like you to become independent,
and assume the leadership of Savis.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:28.160
What are you saying?

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:31.210
What will be left for Lord Theo
if he throws it all away?

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.710
He'll have his reputation!

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:37.130
A young wandering Lord,
appearing from nowhere,

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.720
puts up a valiant fight
against the Knights of Valdrind!

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:45.220
With a luminous reputation like that,
he can mount a comeback anytime.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:47.720
And that's not all I'll get to keep.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:48.720
What else is there?

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.770
I'll still have you.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.350
The mage who'll make my dreams come true.

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:59.110
W-Well, I'm under contract to you,
so that's a given!

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.700
Sir Neyman was killed in action,
and Aishela is gravely injured.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.580
We don't want any more casualties.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:10.830
With our military gains as leverage,

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:14.120
I'll head to Valdrind to propose a ceasefire
before the day is out.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:21.840
Our conditions for a ceasefire
will be Lord Theo's life.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:23.090
No way...

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:25.680
As the King of Savis is now dead,

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:29.220
all the blame for this battle
will be leveled at the Knights of Valdrind.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:32.600
Therefore, the Knights have no room
for compromise.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.230
You fought a splendid battle.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:38.440
However, once again,
you've overplayed your hand.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.240
So the talks broke down, huh?

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:45.910
To think that they'd call for Lord Theo's life...

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.160
I don't understand!

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.750
Lord Theo fought gallantly,
and did everything the right way!

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:56.460
But this way, your lives and standings
will definitely be safe. So...

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.380
With terms like that,
we'd never accept them!

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:03.510
- We'd never abandon you, Lord Theo!
- We'll fight till the end!

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:08.090
Please forgive me for my incompetence.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:11.890
No. Ever since I met you,
I've lived life to the fullest.

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.520
I'm sad to see my dream come to an end,

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:18.650
but the satisfaction of pursuing it is greater.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:21.150
Thank you.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:30.780
Lord Theo was prepared to be stripped
of all but a Knight's court rank,

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.870
and resume his life as a wanderer.

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.750
I believe we could've
accepted those terms for a ceasefire.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:43.250
If we end it here, there may be rumors
that the Knights of Valdrind were defeated.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.670
If so, we would lose face as warriors.

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:49.680
If we surround them in full force, we can level
that broken-down castle in one fell swoop!

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:54.100
Under that plan, we would be unable
to protect Lady Marrine.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:57.600
The Earl of Artuk's mercenaries
turn up when you least expect.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.690
They may be lurking
near the battlefield as we speak.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.190
The Earl of Artuk won't make a move.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.070
He sent that mage Siluca packing, after all.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:07.700
I see...

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:10.490
So you're all convinced
Artuk won't make a move.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:14.330
Wouldn't you say that's precisely
the best time to strike?

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:19.670
Th-Then we'll leave a hundred men here,
and the remaining forces will attack!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:22.540
No, a mere one hundred men won't do.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.960
Lady Marrine, your approval!

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.050
May I ask one thing?

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:32.010
What is it that you fight for?

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.310
For the Kreische family's crest, of course.

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:37.230
Very well, then.

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:40.980
You say it would cause you to lose face.

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:42.980
And if that is your reason,

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:46.820
I would've thought the Kreische
family crest meant nothing to you.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.660
You Lords may fight as you see fit.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:54.160
As you wish!

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.790
We swear on
the Hammer of the Kreische clan!

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:07.170
They sure didn't leave many men
at their stronghold.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:11.050
They must be sure that the Earl of Artuk
won't come to our aid.

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.430
Do you really think the earl won't show up?

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.560
Yes. I was told he wouldn't.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:20.440
That the earl had no intention
of meeting with me now...

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:22.810
Not now?

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:27.230
If the Earl of Artuk has been waiting
for this exact moment...

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.120
Is that the Earl of Artuk's forces?

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:45.630
Absurd! No way reinforcements are coming!

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.430
There she is!
Marrine Kreische is here!

00:16:58.390 --> 00:16:59.220
Villar...

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:02.310
Hey, there...

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:04.600
My dear cousin.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:10.190
Head back to the stronghold
to aid Lady Marrine!

00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:12.110
Fall back! Fall back!

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.110
Sir Theo!

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:13.570
Whoa!

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.100
Aishela!

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:47.900
Thank goodness!

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.440
I wouldn't know what I'd do
if you never woke up again!

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.360
I thought I was a goner, too.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.820
It's all thanks to Priscilla!

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:04.040
If you can heal wounds that serious,
then as I thought, you must be Farnese's G-

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.250
It was all God's will!

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.340
Th-Thanks.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:13.470
Here's my report.

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:16.300
The Knights of Valdrind
suffered immense casualties.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:19.970
They must've decided that
further combat would be ill-advised,

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:21.720
as the entire force is in retreat.

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:23.850
Guess we found a way out of that jam!

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:28.900
That said, under no circumstances
is the Earl of Artuk our ally.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:30.690
There's no telling how he'll deal with you.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:33.360
Speaking of the Earl of Artuk...

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.490
Pardon me!

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:46.500
So you're Lord Theo, huh?

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:48.670
I watched you guys in battle.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.920
I'd like to pay my utmost respect.

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:56.800
I'm sincerely grateful to you
for saving us in our time of crisis.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:59.640
Don't mention it.
It wasn't only for your sake.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.100
I might have let Marrine get away,

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.890
but in terms of military gains,
we did good.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.400
Now, I'd like to discuss
the next steps with you...

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:09.310
Your Lordship!

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:12.440
First allow me to apologize
for my numerous affronts!

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:17.900
What's this?
I see no reason for you to apologize.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:18.570
What?

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:23.990
You entered into a contract with me,
and carried out your mission splendidly, yes?

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:27.960
You threw Savis into a state of disorder,
and pried it away from the Alliance.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:32.090
Therefore, the Mage Academy no longer
has any reason to penalize you,

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:37.050
and I can now welcome
a superior mage into my ranks.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:39.760
W-Well...

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:42.600
Then what will happen to Lord Theo?

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:46.390
Well, Lord Theo will become
the leader of Savis.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:48.810
I won't ask him to serve me.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:52.690
Let's join forces in this battle,
as Union comrades!

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:59.530
King of Savis, Viscount Theo Cornaro...

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.780
All hail!

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.160
All hail!

00:20:05.990 --> 00:20:07.160
I cannot agree to that.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:12.170
You have other conditions, perhaps?

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:16.170
I'd like to pledge my allegiance
to you as a knight.

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:20.050
I'm content having a high enough
court rank to employ Siluca.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:23.010
What's he talking about?

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:26.390
Most likely, he won't relinquish Siluca.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:30.390
However, since that would be the same as
disregarding your kindness,

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:32.400
he is willing to serve you.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.650
Not like the guy matters to me at all.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:39.990
I sense he is a different kind of man
than the Lords under your control.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:44.160
Along with Siluca Meletes,
I'm sure you'll find him useful.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.160
Well, if you say so.

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:52.370
Very well, but I won't allocate any territories
to you. You'll be living in my castle.

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:57.550
And Siluca, I'm going to treat you
as one of my own mages, is that acceptable?

00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:59.510
Very well, my lord.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.850
Um... Lord Theo?

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:10.310
Don't say a word. This was my own decision.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:13.440
I'm returning to being a knight,
and leaving this land.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:16.730
I'm handing over
my court rank to you, Lassic.

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:17.900
You sure about that?

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:19.320
It's fine with me.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.360
But that doesn't mean
I'm abandoning my dream.

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:24.570
Someday, I'm going back to my homeland.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:26.030
All right.

00:21:26.030 --> 00:21:29.330
But remember,
my loyalties will always lie with you.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:33.080
If you ever need me,
I'll drop everything to come to your aid.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:33.920
Thanks.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:38.090
I, too, have made a promise
to God to guide you.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:43.340
I'll be joining you in Artuk,
so I look forward to continuing work with you.

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:47.800
If you want to spread the gospel,
I hope you clear it with the earl first.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:51.100
Now that I'm a lowly knight,
with no territories to speak of.

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:55.600
Hey, you'll get more territories in no time!

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:57.110
I hope that's true!

00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:59.770
<i>Could it be that I...</i>

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:05.110
DECISION

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:40.130
EPISODE 5:
FOREST OF ETERNAL DARKNESS
